   "evidence": "The offline probe exercised the actual queue and Factory.createRun method with an in-memory store; githubSh was stubbed, so no network or real gh command ran. HEAD config stores `repos: [...new Set(repos.map((repo) => repo.toLowerCase()))]`. Independently, issue-queue.ts:260\u2013261 lowercases each configured name and passes that value through issueRunRequest to createRun. Store.getRepoBySlug uses `SELECT * FROM repos WHERE slug = ?`; the schema has `slug TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` without NOCASE. resolveRepo retains the requested lowercase slug when inserting the discovered repository, even when the stubbed SSH URL contains the original capitalization. At base, config preserves spelling and the queue acts on that spelling. The separate-cache assertion is filesystem-dependent because case-insensitive filesystems can alias the two cache paths, but the duplicate database row and incorrect policy are reproduced."
